{
  "workflow_id": "pack-agent-payment-compliance-trail",
  "name": "Agent Payment Compliance Trail",
  "outcome": "A nine-stage agent payment workflow over caller-declared data. Step 1 validates the AP2 Intent, Cart and Payment mandate trio for signature-chain integrity, scope and limit consistency, expiry and over-spend (art-01). Step 2 then validates the on-behalf-of mandate the agent acts under, covering subject, scope, intent and validity window (art-151). Step 3 then cross-checks the declared KYA credential scope against the declared x402 payment payload (art-565). Step 4 then scores the declared transaction graph for laundering typologies (art-10). Step 5 then validates travel-rule field completeness across the declared transfer batch (art-104). Step 6 then binds the screening decision to the exact dataset version it was screened against (art-585). Step 7 then verifies the payment receipt against its mandate chain under the human-not-present guardrail (art-62). Step 8 then recomputes the Permit2 settlement digest for the declared payment (art-699). Step 9 aggregates the declared execution hashes of the session into one Merkle-root audit receipt (cry-05). Each step computes from its own declared inputs; the order is analytical, not a statutory sequence, and the workflow certifies nothing.",
